<p>
    <strong>Core Gameplan:</strong> White hatebear decks come at you from two
    angles: a fast clock of protected threats (<a
        role="button" tabindex="0"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Mother of Runes">Mother of Runes</a
    >, <a
        role="button" tabindex="0"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Silver Knight">Silver Knight</a
    >) plus attacking your mana with <a
        role="button" tabindex="0"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Armageddon">Armageddon</a
    >. Fetch basics early so a land wipe hurts less, and save your <a
        role="button" tabindex="0"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Swords to Plowshares"
        >Swords to Plowshares</a
    > for the threats that actually matter—their real clock or a key protective
    creature.
</p>
<p>
    <strong>Sideboard Strategy:</strong> Trim your fragile mana and slow card
    selection. Bring in <a
        role="button" tabindex="0"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Exalted Angel">Exalted Angel</a
    >—an untargetable morph that takes over the board before they can
    Armageddon—along with <a
        role="button" tabindex="0"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Arcane Denial">Arcane Denial</a
    > and defensive spot removal. If you land a creature before Armageddon
    resolves, their whole plan falls apart.
</p>
